NAME
    find - recursively list files and directories

SYNOPSIS
    find [path] [-name pattern]

DESCRIPTION
    Recursively traverses [path] (default: current directory) inside the
    shell sandbox and prints matching entries one per line, preserving
    the path prefix as given.

    When -name is specified, directories whose names do not match are
    still traversed so matching descendants are printed.

OPTIONS
    -name pattern
        Filter entries by base name using a case-insensitive glob
        supporting '*' (any sequence), '?' (any single character), and
        '\' to match the next character literally.

EXAMPLES
    find /Logs
    find /Games -name '*.sfc'
    find /Saves -name '*.srm'

EXIT STATUS
    0   Traversal completed.
    1   Path outside sandbox or path does not exist.

SEE ALSO
    ls(1), grep(1), cd(1), hier(7)
